# Problem PR Detailed Summary

Whenever the user asks to open a PR, prepare a PR, or wants a **PR summary /
description** for a DSA/algo problem branch, **always** provide a detailed
copy-paste markdown body in chat (and use it for `gh pr create` when creating
the PR). Do not wait to be asked for the long form.

## PR title

`{Topic}: add LeetCode {n} ({Problem Name}) {short approach} solution and tests`

Examples:
- `Graphs: add LeetCode 542 (01 Matrix) multi-source BFS solution and tests`
- `Graphs: add LeetCode 130 (Surrounded Regions) border DFS solution and tests`

## Required body sections (in order)

Use this skeleton; fill every section from the actual solution and tests:

````markdown
## Problem

**LeetCode {n}. {Name}** ({Easy|Medium|Hard})

{1–3 sentence restatement of the problem.}

### Examples

```
{1–2 compact input/output examples}
```

### Constraints

- {bullet list from the problem}

## Solution

{Approach name and high-level idea.}

1. **Step…**
2. **Step…**

### Why {this approach}

{1 short paragraph on the key insight / why not the naive alternative.}

### Complexity

- **Time:** …
- **Space:** …

## Files changed

| File | Change |
| --- | --- |
| `src/main/java/com/practice/...` | … |
| `src/test/java/com/practice/...` | … |

## Test coverage

{Full markdown table matching the test-review-summary rule columns:
Group | Test | Input (brief) | Expected | Why it matters.
One row per test.}

## Test plan

- [x] `./mvnw -Dtest={Class}Test test` — {N} tests, 0 failures
- [ ] `./mvnw test` — full suite green
- [ ] LeetCode submission accepted for provided examples

## Notes

- {branch name, commit focus, anything out of scope}
````

## Guidance

- Prefer the long form above over a short “Summary + Test plan only” body.
- Match tone/structure used for prior graph PRs (01 Matrix, Detect Cycles,
  Rotting Oranges).
- Use `/opt/homebrew/bin/gh` for all GitHub CLI calls (see `project-context.mdc`).
  Do not spend turns locating `gh` on PATH.
- If `gh` still fails, print title + body for copy-paste and the compare URL:
  `https://github.com/{owner}/{repo}/pull/new/{branch}`.
- Rule/chore-only PRs may use a shorter Summary + Test plan body.
